**Employer:** Uber Technologies, Inc.




**Job Title:** Software Engineer




**Job Location:** San Francisco, California




**Job Type:** Full Time




**Rate of Pay:** $213,512\.00 to $256,215\.00 per Year




You will be eligible to participate in Uber's bonus program, and may be offered other types of comp. You will also be eligible for various benefits. More details can be found at the following link https://www.uber.com/careers/benefits .




**Duties:** Build products that accelerate Uber's progress toward waste reduction and vehicle adoption, establishing and extending microservices to deliver user experiences at scale. Collaborate with others on the team and adjacent teams to quickly prototype new products across all of Uber's flagship mobile apps. Design, develop, and/or test software applications using company technology stack. Apply technical knowledge to evaluate complex data, developments, and projects in order to provide recommendations to resolve technical issues. Support the company's business operations and improve engineering productivity. Build software components that can be integrated into a fully functional software system. Solve production issues in product and system reliability. May telecommute.




Employer will accept a Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering (Any), Information Technology, Mathematics, Physics, or related field, followed by five years of progressive, post\-baccalaureate experience in the job offered or in a related occupation.




Position requires:  





* C\+\+, Python, Java, C\#, or Go;
* Version control: GIT or Phabricator;
* SQL or MySQL;
* Data structures and algorithms development and functionality;
* Designing technology stacks;
* Debugging and monitoring for production services;
* Distributed systems and services;
* Software Development Lifecycle.

**Employer:** Uber Technologies, Inc.




**Job Title:** Software Engineer I




**Job Location:** Sunnyvale, California




**Job Type:** Full Time




**Rate of Pay:** $153,000 to $169,000 per Year




You will be eligible to participate in Uber's bonus program, and may be offered other types of comp. You will also be eligible for various benefits. More details can be found at the following link https://www.uber.com/careers/benefits .




**Duties:** Design, develop, and test software applications. Design, develop, and/or test software applications using company technology stack. Apply technical knowledge to evaluate complex data, developments, and projects in order to provide recommendations to resolve technical issues. Support the company's business operations and improve engineering productivity. Build software components that can be integrated into a fully functional software system. Solve production issues in product and system reliability. May telecommute.




Employer will accept a Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering (Any), Information Technology, Mathematics, Physics, or related field, and one year of experience in the job offered or in a related occupation.




Position requires one year in:


* C\+\+, Python, Java, GIT, or SVN;
* Data structures and algorithms development and functionality;
* Designing technology stacks;
* Debugging and monitoring for production services;
* Distributed systems;
* Software Development Lifecycle;
* CI/CD (Continuous Integration/Continuous Delivery or Deployment) systems;
* Unit and integration tests.

**Employer:** Uber Technologies, Inc.




**Job Title:** Software Engineer II




**Job Location:** Sunnyvale, California




**Job Type:** Full Time




**Rate of Pay:** $226,138 to $271,366 per Year




You will be eligible to participate in Uber's bonus program, and may be offered other types of comp. You will also be eligible for various benefits. More details can be found at the following link https://www.uber.com/careers/benefits .




**Duties:** Design, develop, and test software applications. Design, develop, and/or test software applications using company technology stack. Apply technical knowledge to evaluate complex data, developments, and projects in order to provide recommendations to resolve technical issues. Support the company's business operations and improve engineering productivity. Build software components that can be integrated into a fully functional software system. Solve production issues in product and system reliability. May telecommute.




Employer will accept a Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering (Any), Information Technology, Mathematics, Physics, or related field, and four years of experience in the job offered or in a related occupation. OR employer will accept a Master's degree in Computer Science, Engineering (Any), Information Technology, Mathematics, Physics, or related field, and two years of experience in the job offered or in a related occupation.




Position requires:


* Frontend web development using JavaScript, HTML5, and CSS, including experience with modern frontend frameworks such as server\-driven UIs;
* Backend development building scalable services using Java or Go;
* Relational databases and SQL, including data modeling and query optimization;
* Distributed systems fundamentals, including service reliability, scalability, and performance considerations;
* Version control systems (Git), including code reviews and collaborative development workflows;
* Web application performance optimization, including frontend rendering and backend response latency;
* Software testing and debugging, including unit tests and integration tests;
* RESTful API integration and client\-server communication, including JSON\-based data exchange and error handling;
* Troubleshooting and resolving production issues in web applications, including root cause analysis and system reliability improvements.

**Employer:** Uber Technologies, Inc.




**Job Title:** Sr Software Engineer




**Job Location:** Sunnyvale, California




**Job Type:** Full Time




**Rate of Pay:** $264,514 to $317,417 per Year




You will be eligible to participate in Uber's bonus program, and may be offered other types of comp. You will also be eligible for various benefits. More details can be found at the following link https://www.uber.com/careers/benefits .




**Duties:** Partner with stakeholders and support team efforts to design, develop, and maintain complex user interfaces and features for mobile applications (Android). Design, develop, and/or test software applications using company technology stack. Apply technical knowledge to evaluate complex data, developments, and projects in order to provide recommendations to resolve technical issues. Support the company's business operations and improve engineering productivity. Build software components that can be integrated into a fully functional software system. Solve production issues in product and system reliability. May telecommute.




Employer will accept a Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering (Any), Information Technology, Mathematics, Physics, or related field, followed by five years of progressive, post\-baccalaureate experience in the job offered or in a related occupation.




Position requires:


* Mobile Infrastructure and Platform Engineering;
* Android Development;
* Bazel or Gradle Build Tooling;
* Mobile Performance Optimization;
* Mobile telemetry architecture and instrumentation;
* Kotlin and Java;
* Data structures and algorithms development;
* Git/Software Version Control.
